      "writtenOn": "2020-08-07T22:40:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I attached the Twinkie capture to the bug. Index 77 is the soft reset.\n\nSo it looks like we barely meet timing in the real world, and we could/should probably do better.\n\nI think the difference here, is that the TCPC is responding with a FAILURE status and then our state machine responds to that. In this test we are letting hte 100 msec TCPC timeout expire (which isn\u0027t what is happening in real life).\n\nSo to make the test more accurate, we should set the mock a TC_COMPLETE that is a failure. See https://source.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/driver/tcpm/tcpci.c;l\u003d1143?q\u003df:platform%2Fec%20TCPC_REG_ALERT_RX_STATUS\u0026sq\u003dpackage:(%5Echromeos_internal$%7C%5Echromeos_public$)\u0026type\u003dcs",
